# Both images build from the repository root, because the workspaces in
# `packages/` are real dependencies of both apps and a context scoped to
# `apps/api` or `apps/web` could not see them. That makes this file the only
# thing standing between a developer's working tree and a deployed image.

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# First, and deny-all like `.gitignore`'s equivalent rule: `apps/api/.env` holds
# a live database URL, the Better Auth secret, the webhook password and an
# OpenAI key. Every one of those is supplied by Railway at runtime instead, so
# an .env reaching an image is pure downside — and a layer is readable by
# anyone who can pull the image, whether or not the process ever loads it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
.npmrc
.netrc

# --- Dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------
# Installed inside the image against the lockfile. Copying a host `node_modules`
# in would also drag Windows-built native binaries into a Linux image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Regenerated by `prisma generate` during the API build, for the image's own
# platform.
apps/api/src/generated

# --- Version control and tooling --------------------------------------------
# Excluding `.git` means `releaseName()` in vite.config.ts cannot ask git for a
# commit and falls back to `web@0.0.0` — which that function is written to
# tolerate. Pass VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE from RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA instead; see
# DEPLOYMENT.md.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.agents
.vscode

# --- Tests and reports ------------------------------------------------------
tests
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright
playwright.config.ts

# --- Docs and local scratch -------------------------------------------------
**/*.md
# The seed corpus for a fresh deployment (`bun run db:seed:kb`). Not read at
# runtime — the knowledge base is a table — but the image is where the seed is
# run from.
!apps/api/knowledge-base.md
scripts
*.log
